.TH ARCHR 7 "2026-06-23" "ArchR" "ArchR Manual"
.SH NAME
archr \- overview of the ArchR distribution
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ArchR
is a Linux distribution targeted at the Rockchip RK3326 handheld console family
(R36S, K36, MagicX XU10, Soysauce/Y3506 and clones).
It boots from a microSD card, runs archr-launcher as its front end,
and ships a curated catalogue of emulators, RetroAchievements integration,
PortMaster compatibility and panel auto-detection via DTBO overlays.
.PP
ArchR follows the Arch Linux family conventions (
.BR ID_LIKE =arch
in
.IR /etc/os-release ", "
empty sentinel file at
.IR /etc/archr-release )
while keeping the LibreELEC-inherited boot model: read-only squashfs rootfs
plus a read-write overlay at
.IR /storage .
This combination is shared with SteamOS and chosen for its resilience to
power-loss during gameplay and for atomic system updates.
.SH COMMANDS
The following helpers are installed under
.IR /usr/bin
and are the public interface of the distro:
.TP
.B archr-update
Check for and apply an OS update with
.B pacman -Syu
against the channel in
.I updates.branch
(stable, next or dev).
.B check --json
and
.B update --progress
are the machine interface archr-launcher uses; the script header documents it.
The log is
.IR /storage/.config/archr-update.log .
.TP
.B archr-config
Read or write a runtime setting persisted in
.IR /storage/.config/system/configs/system.cfg .
Used by every emulator launcher and by archr-launcher.
.TP
.B archr-settings
Top-level settings dispatcher for the user interface.
.TP
.B archr-systems
List supported emulator systems and their associated cores.
.TP
.B archr-scraper
Scrape metadata and box art for the games library.
.TP
.B archr-info
Show device, firmware, kernel, panel overlay and GPU driver in use.
.TP
.B archr-keyboard
Toggle the on-screen virtual keyboard.
.TP
.B archr-bluetooth ", " archr-bluetooth-agent
Manage Bluetooth devices and the agent that pairs them headlessly.
.TP
.B archr-memory-manager
Configure zram, swappiness and the OOM behaviour. Started as a service at boot.
.TP
.B archr-report-stats
Send anonymized telemetry when the user opts in.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
ArchR scripts read filesystem paths through the
.B ARCHR_*
family of variables, exported by
.IR /etc/profile.d/010-archr-fhs .
This vocabulary is stable; the underlying paths migrate to FHS locations
across releases (see
.IR docs/fhs-mapping.md
in the source tree). Callers should never hardcode
.IR /storage/.config
or its siblings; use the variable instead.
.TP
.B ARCHR_ETC
System configuration. Currently
.IR /storage/.config ;
target
.IR /etc/archr .
.TP
.B ARCHR_CONFIG
User and application configuration (emulators, archr-launcher,
PortMaster). Resolves to
.IR /var/lib/archr/config ,
a symlink into
.IR /storage/.config
on the rw overlay.
.TP
.B ARCHR_CACHE
Regenerable cache (shader cache, fontconfig, service state). Currently
.IR /storage/.cache ;
target
.IR /var/cache/archr .
.TP
.B ARCHR_DATA
Persistent state and data. Resolves to
.IR /var/lib/archr/data ,
a symlink into
.IR /storage/.local/share
on the rw overlay.
.TP
.B ARCHR_GAMES
Games library root (ROMs, saves, screenshots, recordings). Resolves
to
.IR /var/lib/archr/games ,
a symlink into
.IR /storage/roms
on the rw overlay.
.TP
.B ARCHR_LOG
Log files. Currently
.IR /storage/.cache/log ;
target
.IR /var/log/archr .
.TP
.B ARCHR_TMP
Ephemeral temp. Currently
.IR /storage/.tmp ;
target
.IR /var/tmp/archr .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/os-release
Distribution identity (NAME, ID, ID_LIKE, VERSION_ID).
.TP
.I /etc/archr-release
Empty sentinel file. Detected by third-party tools to recognize ArchR as Arch
family. Equivalent to
.IR /etc/arch-release
on Arch Linux.
.TP
.I /storage/.config
User-writable configuration root for emulators, archr-launcher, system
preferences and saved settings.
.TP
.I /storage/roms
Default ROM library root: one folder per system, as in the systems catalog.
.TP
.I /usr/share/bootloader
Boot files installed by mkimage: kernel, DTB, overlay catalogue, update script.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/archr.target
Default systemd target. Symlinks
.IR default.target
into it during build.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd (1),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR archr-update (1)
.PP
